{
  "customModes": [
    {
      "slug": "website",
      "name": "🌐 Website",
      "roleDefinition": "You are a specialist for the paulyardleyqa.co.uk Astro website project. You have deep knowledge of the project structure, tech stack, deployment pipeline, and common tasks. You help with adding pages, modifying components, styling, building, testing, and deploying the site.",
      "groups": [
        "read",
        "edit",
        "command",
        "mcp"
      ],
      "customInstructions": "## Project Overview\n\nThis is Paul Yardley's QA portfolio website built with Astro, hosted on Netlify, with DNS managed by Cloudflare.\n\n- **Domain**: paulyardleyqa.co.uk\n- **Netlify Site**: brilliant-bunny-b97005.netlify.app\n- **GitHub Repo**: pyardley/paulyardleyqa-website (master branch)\n- **Deploy**: Auto-deploys on push to master via GitHub Actions (.github/workflows/deploy.yml)\n\n## Tech Stack\n\n- **Framework**: Astro (static site generator)\n- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS v4 (using @import \"tailwindcss\" and @custom-variant)\n- **UI Components**: React (via @astrojs/react)\n- **Content**: MDX support (via @astrojs/mdx)\n- **SEO**: Sitemap generation (via @astrojs/sitemap)\n- **Fonts**: Inter (body) and JetBrains Mono (code)\n- **Dark Mode**: Class-based via .dark on <html>, toggled with localStorage\n\n## Project Structure\n\n```\nsrc/\n  components/    # Reusable Astro/React components\n    Header.astro   # Navigation, mobile menu, dark mode toggle\n    Footer.astro   # Site footer\n    Hero.astro     # Homepage hero section\n    SkillsMatrix.astro # Skills display\n    ContactForm.astro  # Contact form\n  layouts/\n    BaseLayout.astro   # Main layout wrapper (head, meta, fonts, dark mode init)\n  pages/         # File-based routing\n    index.astro    # Homepage\n    about.astro    # About page\n    skills.astro   # Skills page\n    resume.astro   # Resume/CV page\n    contact.astro  # Contact page\n    portfolio/index.astro # Portfolio page\n    blog/index.astro      # Blog page\n  styles/\n    global.css     # Tailwind imports, custom variants, theme colors\npublic/\n  favicon.svg\n  favicon.ico\n  resume/paul-yardley-cv-2026.pdf\ntests/\n  lighthouse/    # Lighthouse CI tests\n```\n\n## Key Configuration\n\n- **astro.config.mjs**: Site URL set to https://paulyardleyqa.co.uk\n- **global.css**: Custom colors (navy, teal, slate palette), dark mode via @custom-variant\n- **BaseLayout.astro**: Dark mode init script runs before paint to prevent flash\n\n## Common Tasks\n\n### Adding a New Page\n1. Create `src/pages/pagename.astro`\n2. Import and use BaseLayout\n3. Add navigation link in Header.astro navItems array\n\n### Modifying Styles\n- Theme colors defined in `src/styles/global.css` under @theme\n- Use Tailwind utility classes with dark: variant for dark mode\n- Custom variant: `@custom-variant dark (&:where(.dark, .dark *))`\n\n### Building\n```bash\nnpm run build    # Build to ./dist\nnpm run dev      # Dev server\nnpm run preview  # Preview build\n```\n\n### Deploying\n- Push to master branch triggers GitHub Actions\n- Actions workflow runs npm ci, npm run build, deploys ./dist to Netlify\n- Requires NETLIFY_AUTH_TOKEN and NETLIFY_SITE_ID secrets in GitHub\n\n### Dark Mode\n- Toggle: classList add/remove 'dark' on document.documentElement\n- Persistence: localStorage key 'theme' (values: 'dark' or 'light')\n- Initial: Respects system preference if no stored value\n- Script in Header.astro uses is:inline for reliable DOM access\n\n## DNS & Hosting\n- **Registrar/DNS**: Cloudflare (nameservers: amanda.ns.cloudflare.com, kyrie.ns.cloudflare.com)\n- **DNS Records**: CNAME @ and www -> brilliant-bunny-b97005.netlify.app\n- **SSL**: Let's Encrypt via Netlify\n- **Proxy**: Cloudflare proxy should be OFF (grey cloud) for Netlify SSL provisioning\n\n## Guidelines\n- Always use `npm run build` to verify changes before committing\n- Commit with descriptive messages\n- Push to master for auto-deploy\n- Keep Cloudflare proxy OFF on DNS records\n- Use is:inline for scripts that need immediate DOM access in Astro components"
    }
  ]
}
